# allow-hosts-blocked.tflw — DEMO-FAIL FIXTURE (M23, testFlow PLAN.md decision 101a; reshaped for
# tflw M85 / review cluster C1): the negative case for `allow hosts` — a request to a real,
# reachable host that just isn't on the allowlist must be refused before any network I/O, not
# silently let through. Run under `--env allowHostsBlocked` (tflw.config).
#
# The blocked host arrives by *redirect*, which is both the honest shape of the risk and the only
# one still expressible: the dangerous host in practice is one the server picks, not one anybody
# typed, and since M85 an env whose own base URL its own allowlist excludes is a `tflw check` error
# (`TF036`) — so this fixture's old shape would now prove the checker rather than the guardrail.
# `/safety-demo/offsite-redirect` 302s to `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1/health`: the same server,
# spelled as a different host, healthy and listening. The request *would* have succeeded; it is
# refused at the hop instead, so `expect status equals 200` never gets an answer.
#
# Run explicitly (dot-directory, invisible to a bare `tflw run`/`tflw check`):
#   npx tflw run tests/.demo-fail/allow-hosts-blocked.tflw --env allowHostsBlocked --tag demofail

@demofail @safety
test "a redirect to a host outside `allow hosts` is refused before it ever reaches the real, healthy server"
  api GET /safety-demo/offsite-redirect
  expect status equals 200
